From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 20:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: regulator: da9211: make interrupts optional

The DA9211 regulator driver already treats client->irq == 0 as a
supported configuration: it registers the regulators, skips the
over-current IRQ setup, and emits a warning.  The binding nevertheless
requires an interrupt for all
DA9211--DA9215 and DA9223--DA9225 variants.

Some boards use these regulators without wiring the interrupt.  Make the
property optional so the schema describes the driver's existing contract.
When present, the interrupt continues to have the same one-item constraint.

---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/dlg,da9211.yaml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/dlg,da9211.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/dlg,da9211.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/dlg,da9211.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/dlg,da9211.yaml
@@ -62,6 +62,5 @@ required:
   - compatible
   - reg
-  - interrupts
   - regulators
 
 additionalProperties: false
-- 
2.43.0
